# User-journey diagram governance

When a change affects a user journey documented in [`docs/app-flows.md`](docs/app-flows.md)
(screens/routes/CTAs/scan-transfer/CSV behavior that users experience):

1. Read [`docs/app-flows.md`](docs/app-flows.md) first.
2. Do **not** edit journey diagrams in the same dirty working tree as screen/code changes.
3. Do **not** create git commits. Wait until the user has committed the tested code.
4. After that commit is on HEAD, update diagrams (optionally via the update skill).
   Put diagram edits in a later `Docs` change; the user decides when to commit it.

Skip if the change is unrelated to documented journeys.

Bootstrap exception: creating/updating `docs/app-flows.md` itself is allowed to establish the first map.
